---
title: Specimen Parts
sidebar:
  label: Specimen parts
  order: 6
---

Use `Specimen Parts` for voucher preparations, tissues, swabs, and other
physical parts derived from a specimen. Each specimen can have multiple parts.
Organisms found living on or in a host specimen are recorded separately as
[symbionts](/en/usages/specimens/symbionts/).

The `Specimen Parts` card uses icon tabs:

- **Catalog icon**: specimen parts.
- **Bug icon**: [symbionts](/en/usages/specimens/symbionts/) (shown for
  `Mammalogy`, `Ornithology`, `Herpetology`, and `Ichthyology`).
- **Storage icon**:
  [associated data](/en/usages/specimens/associated-data-and-media/).

For a fish lot with recorded individuals, parts and symbionts can be linked to
the individuals they came from; see
[Fishes](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/fishes/#parts-and-symbionts).

Default part fields:

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `Tissue ID` | Optional. While empty, the repeat icon copies the last tissue ID entered for this specimen. `Tissue ID options` offers `New number` (takes the next configured tissue number) and `Settings`. |
| `QR/barcode ID` | Optional unique ID for a tube, tag, or container. `QR/barcode ID options` offers `Scan QR/Barcode` (on devices with a camera) and `Generate UUID`. |
| `Individuals` | Shown only for a fish lot with recorded individuals. Links the part to individuals in the lot. |
| `Preparation type` | From your `Specimen Types` controlled vocabulary. Choosing a type sets `Counts` to `1` if empty. |
| `Counts` | Number of parts or containers. |
| `Treatment` | Preservation treatment from your `Treatments` controlled vocabulary. |
| `Time taken` | When the part was taken; recommended for fresh tissues. |

Additional fields shown after `Show more` (and, except for
`Additional treatment`, automatically shown when they hold a value):

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `Additional treatment` | Secondary preservation treatment from `Treatments`. Shown after `Show more`. |
| `Preparator` | When different from the voucher's preparator. |
| `Date taken` | When the part was taken. |
| `PMI` | Post-mortem interval, such as `1:30`. |
| `Storage type`, `Storage location` | Storage medium and freezer, cabinet, shelf, cell, or jar position. |
| `Museum permanent`, `Museum loan` | The museum holding the part, and one receiving it on loan. |
| `Remarks` | Notes specific to this part. |

Custom fields configured for specimen parts appear at the end of the form.

Each row in the part list displays the part icon, type, count, preparator,
barcode ID, linked fish individuals, tissue ID, treatments, date and time
taken, PMI, and whether a remark is present. Use the edit icon to update a part,
or turn on selection mode to delete parts.

## Symbionts

Symbiont records, examination fields, settings, curation, and exports have
their own page: [Symbionts](/en/usages/specimens/symbionts/).
